# =============================================================================
# Day 20 — .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# Everything here is excluded from the BUILD CONTEXT — the archive Docker sends
# to the daemon before the first instruction runs. This matters for three
# reasons:
#
#   1. SPEED. Without it, `docker build` uploads your .venv, .git history and
#      every database file. That is often hundreds of megabytes, on every build.
#   2. CACHING. A change to any file in the context can invalidate cached
#      layers, so an untracked log file causes a full rebuild.
#   3. SECURITY. `COPY . .` copies .env and .git — and a .git directory in a
#      shipped image contains every secret you ever committed and removed.
#
# Writing this file BEFORE the Dockerfile is the right order.
# =============================================================================

.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

# Secrets — never in an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local state
instance/
*.db
*.sqlite3
uploads/
logs/

# Dev tooling
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
tests/
requirements-dev.txt

# Editors / OS
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Docs and compose files are not needed inside the image
README.md
docker-compose.yml
